3","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113474#issuecomment-4832890393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113474","id":4832890393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIBAOGQ","user":{"login":"marmitoTH","id":25598040,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NTk4MDQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25598040?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH","html_url":"https://github.com/marmitoTH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marmitoTH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-29T13:02:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-29T13:02:08Z","body":"Same problem here! Setting FOV Override to false fixes the blocky artifacts. v4.6.3.stable.official.\n\n<img width=\"1143\" height=\"643\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c456057f-1e1d-4d15-8c0e-7d9a50e921bc\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4832890393/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4965213035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113474#issuecomment-4965213035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113474","id":4965213035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ_Mjaw","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T03:49:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T03:49:52Z","body":"This happens as a side effect of the way clustering works. I'm not sure there is any foolproof way to avoid this entirely since clustering relies on the camera's projection matrix. When you modify the FOV for the single object it ends up in a very different screen space position so it no longer aligns with the camera projection. \n\nThe problem is worse with a few situations:\n1. Objects that are far away from the camera will stray further\n2. The greater the difference in FOV is between the camera and the object\n3. The smaller the area of the light cluster. (i.e. the smaller the light angle and range)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4965213035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159592212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113474#issuecomment-5159592212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113474","id":5159592212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM4khFA","user":{"login":"that404nerd","id":68456596,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NDU2NTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68456596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd","html_url":"https://github.com/that404nerd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/that404nerd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T17:48:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T17:52:23Z","body":"\n> This happens as a side effect of the way clustering works. I'm not sure there is any foolproof way to avoid this entirely since clustering relies on the camera's projection matrix. When you modify the FOV for the single object it ends up in a very different screen space position so it no longer aligns with the camera projection.\n> \n> The problem is worse with a few situations:\n> \n> 1. Objects that are far away from the camera will stray further\n> 2. The greater the difference in FOV is between the camera and the object\n> 3. The smaller the area of the light cluster. (i.e. the smaller the light angle and range)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/43346983-052f-4f1a-8090-203969b6508d\n\nAs you can see, the farther I move away from the mesh, the more it seems to offset. And it only happens if FOV override is enabled. If disabled it doesn't happen at all. \n\nEngine Version: 4.7.1","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5159592212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]